# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file — every value
# below is a live credential.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Email ---
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RESEND_FROM=onenight <noreply@your-domain.com>

# --------------------------------------------------------------- Database ---
# Supabase Postgres. Pooled (PgBouncer, port 6543) at runtime; direct
# (port 5432) for migrations.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Storage ---
# Used by src/dresses/storage.service.ts to upload listing photos.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project API keys → service_role
# SECRET: bypasses RLS. Server-side only — never put it in frontend/.env,
# since anything VITE_-prefixed is compiled into the browser bundle.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --------------------------------------------------------------- AI photos ---
# Admin-only AI product photography (src/dresses/ai-photo.service.ts): turns a
# listing photo of a dress into a photo of a person wearing it, via FASHN's
# `product-to-model` endpoint.

# FASHN API key — https://app.fashn.ai/api
# SECRET and metered: billed in FASHN credits. The service pins the cheapest
# tier explicitly (generation_mode: fast, resolution: 1k) = 1 credit per image.
# Server-side only.
# This is a FASHN account key, NOT a fal.ai key; the two are unrelated.
FASHN_API_KEY=

# Optional — pin a different FASHN model. Defaults to product-to-model.
# Only swap in another SINGLE-input model: try-on models additionally require a
# model_image (a photo of a person), which this service does not send.
# FASHN_MODEL_NAME=

# Optional — art direction for every generated photo: who the model is, the
# pose, the backdrop, the lighting. This single string decides the look of the
# whole catalog, so tune it by looking at results rather than in the abstract.
# Defaults to DEFAULT_STUDIO_PROMPT in src/dresses/ai-photo.service.ts, which
# asks for a full-body shot on a seamless cream-white (#FAF6F1) backdrop with
# soft even lighting. Must be one line — leave it unset rather than blank.
# FASHN_STUDIO_PROMPT=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Admin ---
# Shared password for the moderation panel. Demo-grade — no sessions, no rate
# limiting. Defaults to if unset.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
